{
  "raw": {
    "https://www.chowan.edu/about/offices/human-resources/?gnk=job&gni=8a78839e9eb34c42019ed1e13cf61424&lang=en": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Criminal Justice",
      "description": "Position: Assistant Professor of Criminal Justice Location: Murfreesboro, NC Job Id: 181 # of Openings: 1 JOB SUMMARY Chowan University invites applications for a full-time, in-person, 9-month faculty appointment in the Department of Criminal Justice. The appointment will be made at the rank of Assistant Professor (tenure-track) or Instructor (non-tenure track), depending on the qualifications of the successful candidate. ESSENTIAL FUNCTIONS Commitment to excellence in undergraduate teaching and academic advising Ability to integrate technology and innovative teaching methods into the curriculum. Willingness to collaborate with colleagues to enhance academic programs. REQUIRED KNOWLEDGE, SKILLS, AND ABILITIES Excellent verbal and written communication skills. Ability to integrate technology and innovative teaching methods into the curriculum. Willingness to collaborate with colleagues to enhance academic programs. Excellent organizational skills and attention to detail. Excellent time management skills with a proven ability to meet deadlines. Ability to prioritize tasks and to delegate them when appropriate. Ability to function well in a high-paced and at times stressful environment. Demonstrated ability to coordinate and handle multiple tasks simultaneously Excellent interpersonal skills, both written and oral Commitment to the mission of a Christian university and student success. EDUCATION AND EXPERIENCE A Master’s in Criminal Justice or related field is required. A Ph. D. in Criminal Justice is preferred. Experience teaching at the university level is preferred. Apply for this Position Apply with Indeed Go back to the job list powered by"
    },
    "https://www.chowan.edu/about/offices/human-resources/?gnk=job&gni=8a78879e9fd3ba5c01a02f6e56b04705&lang=en": {
      "title": "Director of Career and Community Engagement",
      "description": "Position: Director of Career and Community Engagement Location: Murfreesboro, NC Job Id: 193 # of Openings: 1 JOB SUMMARY The Director of Career and Community Engagement plays a pivotal role in preparing Chowan University students for life beyond the classroom by connecting them to meaningful internships, career pathways, and service opportunities. This position bridges academics, student life, and advancement by cultivating partnerships with employers, community organizations, and alumni. Through collaboration with admissions, student activities, advancement, and alumni relations, the coordinator strengthens the student experience from enrollment through post-graduation, ensuring that every Chowan student is equipped, connected, and supported for career and life success. ESSENTIAL FUNCTIONS Build and maintain partnerships with companies, industries, and professional organizations to secure job opportunities, internships, and mentorships for students. Serve as a liaison between the university and employers to gather insights on workforce needs and align university programs accordingly. Manage a portfolio of employer and community partners and oversee a job and internship database for students and alumni. Coordinate career counseling and support for students, including job search strategies, and interviewing techniques. Collaborate with the Writing Center to promote and support resume and cover letter development as part of students’ broader writing and professional communication skills. Develop and lead individual and group workshops focused on professional development and career readiness. Collaborate with faculty and academic departments to connect classroom learning with real world experiences. Work with Student Activities to create community service and outreach programs that enhance student learning and deepen Chowan’s connection to the local community. Partner with the Advancement Office to cultivate business and industry relationships that may lead to both student support opportunities and philanthropic engagement. Support Admissions by highlighting career development as a distinctive component of the Chowan experience and engaging with prospective students and families. Develop career exposure opportunities, including employer visits, networking events, and on-campus recruiting programs. Represent the university at industry panels, and community events to promote student talent and academic programs. Collect and analyze data on employer engagement, and market trends to inform strategic decisions and continuous improvement. Maintain ongoing communication with recent graduates, serving as a conduit for early alumni engagement and post-graduation support. Develop career exposure and community engagement opportunities, including employer visits, networking events, on-campus recruiting programs, community-based learning experiences, and opportunities for students to engage with local organizations. Represent the University at industry panels, career fairs, civic meetings, community events, and other external engagements to promote student talent, academic programs, and Chowan’s role as an engaged community partner. Collect and analyze data on employer and community partner engagement, student participation, workforce and market trends, and other relevant outcomes to inform strategic decisions and continuous improvement. Maintain ongoing communication with recent graduates, serving as a conduit for early alumni engagement, post-graduation support, career development, and opportunities for alumni to connect with and support current students. REQUIRED KNOWLEDGE, SKILLS, AND ABILITIES Strong understanding of career counseling, job readiness programming, internship coordination, and workforce trends. Proven ability to build and maintain relationships with employers, community organizations, and business leaders for the benefit of students and the university. Ability to work cross-functionally with departments such as Admissions, Student Activities, Advancement, and Alumni Relations. Excellent written and verbal communication skills, with the ability to present to diverse audiences including students, faculty, employers, and donors. Demonstrated commitment to student success, development, and long-term engagement. Skilled in organizing events such as career fairs, community service projects, and employer visits. Familiarity with career platforms (e.g., Handshake, Symplicity), Microsoft Office Suite, CRM systems, and social media for professional engagement. Understanding of how to maintain professional relationships with alumni and donors in support of university advancement and student opportunities. EDUCATION AND EXPERIENCE Bachelor’s degree in Higher Education, Business, Human Resources, Communication, or a related field. Experience working in a college or university setting preferred. Familiarity with advancement, alumni engagement, or corporate philanthropy preferred. Apply for this Position Go back to the job list powered by"
    },
    "https://www.chowan.edu/about/offices/human-resources/?gnk=job&gni=8a78859f9fd3baa001a0030434c96a6d&lang=en": {
      "title": "Director of Development",
      "description": "Position: Director of Development Location: Murfreesboro, NC Job Id: 191 # of Openings: 1 JOB SUMMARY The Development Director plays a pivotal role in advancing the institution's fundraising efforts and fostering relationships with alumni, donors, and other key stakeholders. Reporting to the Vice President of Enrollment and Advancement, this position oversees the planning and execution of comprehensive development initiatives to support the university's mission, vision, and priorities. The Development Director is responsible for cultivating, soliciting, and stewarding major gifts, while also managing alumni engagement strategies to enhance lifelong connections with the university community. ESSENTIAL FUNCTIONS Plan and implement a comprehensive fundraising program that aligns with annual and long-term institutional goals. Manage a personal portfolio of major gift prospects, guiding them through the donor lifecycle from identification to stewardship. Develop compelling proposals and case statements in partnership with academic and administrative leaders. Coordinate donor stewardship and recognition programs to ensure meaningful and consistent engagement. Organize and lead cultivation and fundraising events designed to deepen donor relationships and expand the base of support. Analyze donor data to evaluate fundraising effectiveness and guide future strategy. Collaborate with university leadership and the development team to prioritize funding needs and ensure alignment with strategic initiatives. Oversee the development budget and allocate resources effectively to maximize impact. Provide leadership and direction for university alumni relations strategies, ensuring strong engagement and pipeline development. Supervise and support the Assistant to the Office of Development and Curator and the Development Coordinator. Foster a collaborative, goal-oriented team environment with a focus on accountability, communication, and professional development. Ensure timely and efficient execution of office operations, donor communications, and event planning. REQUIRED KNOWLEDGE, SKILLS, AND ABILITIES Demonstrated success in securing major gifts from individuals, corporations, and foundations. Strong leadership skills with the ability to motivate and mentor staff to achieve fundraising goals. Excellent communication and interpersonal skills, with the ability to effectively engage and inspire diverse constituencies. Strategic thinker with the ability to develop and implement comprehensive fundraising plans. Knowledge of fundraising best practices, including moves management, donor stewardship, and gift acceptance policies. Experience with fundraising databases and prospect research tools. Ability to work collaboratively with colleagues across departments and functions to achieve shared goals. EDUCATION AND EXPERIENCE Bachelor's degree required, advanced degree preferred. Minimum of five years of progressively responsible experience in fundraising, preferably in higher education or a related nonprofit environment. Ability to coordinate and negotiate. Excellent interpersonal skills both written and oral. Demonstrated presentation ability. Apply for this Position Apply with Indeed Go back to the job list powered by"
    },
    "https://www.chowan.edu/about/offices/human-resources/?gnk=job&gni=8a78859f9d4aea0c019d9234ca0d223e&lang=en": {
      "title": "Assistant Athletic Trainer",
      "description": "Position: Assistant Athletic Trainer Location: Murfreesboro, NC Job Id: 175 # of Openings: 2 JOB SUMMARY To advise the Head Athletic Trainer in developing, coordinating, and administering a comprehensive medical sports program for University athletes. CLASSIFICATION This position is classified full-time staff. ESSENTIAL FUNCTIONS Assist in maintaining a program of preventive physical care for athletic teams; determines and ensures the acquisition of safety equipment and supplies applicable to respective sports; Provide first aid treatment for participants of assigned sports; treats or refers injuries to physicians when appropriate; tapes and treats injuries prior to practices and athletic contests; Counsel and educate athletes on nutrition and other life matters; monitors biomechanics and instructs players and coached on corrections; Advise Head Athletic Trainer as requested and may instruct in an academic setting. OTHER DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES Perform other functions and duties as requested by Head Athletic Trainer, such as, but not limited to: Perform minor maintenance of supplies and equipment; Monitor inventory of supplies on a timely basis. REQUIRED KNOWLEDGE, SKILLS, AND ABILITIES The Assistant Athletic Trainer must possess specific areas of knowledge, skill, and ability to be able to explain and/or demonstrate he/she can perform the essential functions of the job, with or without reasonable accommodation, using some combination of skills and abilities.  Furthermore, he/she must conduct such activities in light of the mission and purpose of Chowan University. PERFORMANCE STANDARDS Performance evaluations are based on the incumbent’s ability to perform, in a timely, accurate, and otherwise positive manner, the essential and marginal functions of this job description.  Proper discharge of duties will be measured in part by the number of mistakes made, the ability to work with other employees, and a demonstrated commitment to fulfilling the mission, purpose, and goals of Chowan University. MINIMUM QUALIFICATIONS AND SKILLS Undergraduate degree required, Masters Degree preferred. NATABOC certification required, NC Athletic Training License required (or eligible). 1-2 years-experience as an athletic trainer. Demonstrated ability to coordinate and handle multiple tasks simultaneously. Strong interpersonal skills. STRENGTH: Medium – physical demand in excess of light work.   May exert up to 20 or 50 pounds of force frequently. Apply for this Position Apply with Indeed Go back to the job list powered by"
    },
    "https://www.chowan.edu/about/offices/human-resources/?gnk=job&gni=8a78879ea06420fb01a081b637466093&lang=en": {
      "title": "Financial Aid Advisor I",
      "description": "Position: Financial Aid Advisor I Location: Murfreesboro, NC Job Id: 196 # of Openings: 2 JOB SUMMARY This position is responsible for counseling and advising students and families on the process to receiving financial aid. The Financial Aid Advisor will help students complete FAFSA, determine eligibility for federal, state and institutional aid for individual programs, and make awards to students. The Advisor will also make adjustments to awards during the year. Work is performed under the supervision of the Director of Financial Aid. ESSENTIAL FUNCTIONS Daily processing of admissions acceptance data and daily FAFSA records; Determination for and request of additional documents needed for awarding student; Conduct verification of student records and identifying conflicting data; Awarding of financial aid; ensures applicants receive assistance in the application process for loans and scholarships; Counsels with students and parents concerning the possibility of financial aid; Conduct outreach including calls, mailing, text and other efforts to assist with record completion; Assists students with timely completion of forms; Maintain outside scholarship records including billing and disbursement of funds; Performs loan & literacy counseling; Participate in admissions & athletic in office visits with prospective students and families; Assist with default management activities; Conduct off campus outreach efforts such as high school nights, and FAFSA Days. OTHER DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES Assists in the preparation of student financial aid awards; including all student populations: undergraduate, graduate, adult degree, residency licensure and part time. Work collaboratively with other department across campus. Participate in University sponsored events. Attend trainings virtually and in person when presented. Serve on committees as appointed. Performs other related duties as required. REQUIRED KNOWLEDGE, SKILLS, AND ABILITIES The incumbent must possess specific areas of knowledge, skill, and ability to be able to explain and/or demonstrate he/she can perform the essential functions of the job, with or without reasonable accommodation, using some combination of skills and abilities.Furthermore, he/she must conduct such activities in light of the mission and purpose of Chowan University. EDUCATION AND EXPERIENCE Bachelor’s Degree required (Masters a plus). 2 years experience in a University environment (Financial Aid or Admissions a plus). Demonstrated ability to coordinate and handle multiple tasks simultaneously. Preferred understanding of Powerfaids and Jenzabar. Ability to use Microsoft Excel. Ability to handle various customer service problems tactfully. Strong interpersonal skills, both written and oral. Ability to work unsupervised. Apply for this Position Apply with Indeed Go back to the job list powered by"
    },
    "https://www.chowan.edu/about/offices/human-resources/?gnk=job&gni=8a7887ac9d02e529019d3065ba680cd5&lang=en": {
      "title": "Maintenance HVAC Technician",
      "description": "Position: Maintenance HVAC Technician Location: Murfreesboro, NC Job Id: 171 # of Openings: 1 JOB SUMMARY The HVAC Technician maintains, repairs, and installs heating, ventilation, and refrigeration systems; maintains electrical systems. ESSENTIAL FUNCTIONS Maintain and repair boilers, compressors, pumps, air handling equipment, fans, blowers, and associated control systems including lubrication, housekeeping, and repair. Repair and maintain split system heat pumps and air conditioning. Troubleshoot and diagnose problems that arise in the HVAC equipment. Maintain and repair water coolers and ice machines; repair and maintain coolers and freezer refrigerant systems. Maintain campus filter replacement and cleaning system. REQUIRED KNOWLEDGE, SKILLS, AND ABILITIES Knowledge of computers to maintain HVAC systems Excellent interpersonal and customer service skills. Excellent attention to detail. Excellent time management skills with a proven ability to meet deadlines. May require walking or standing for long periods. Ability to lift and carry up to 50 lbs. Possess a valid driver’s license with a positive driving record. EDUCATION AND EXPERIENCE High School Diploma or Equivalent desired. At least 1 - 2 years of experience in a maintenance or construction environment. Apply for this Position Apply with Indeed Go back to the job list powered by"
    },
    "https://www.chowan.edu/about/offices/human-resources/?gnk=job&gni=8a7887a8a0abfc8001a0af6d359a2d95&lang=en": {
      "title": "Groundskeeper",
      "description": "Position: Groundskeeper Location: Murfreesboro, NC Job Id: 199 # of Openings: 1 JOB SUMMARY Performs general grounds maintenance tasks involved in the maintenance and care of the Chowan University campus. ESSENTIAL FUNCTIONS Operate light mechanized equipment and participate in a variety of groundskeeping tasks in support of campus grounds maintenance projects. Cut lawn using power mower; services and maintains equipment as required. Pick up trash and debris from campus grounds, buildings streets, walkways, and parking areas. Trim and edge walks and flowerbeds using clippers and edging tools. Prune shrubs and hedges to improve growth, transplant trees, flowers, and bulbs. Perform a variety of manual tasks required for grounds maintenance and landscaping projects; place mulch and remove litter and other debris. Assist in setting up equipment for special events. Assist craft workers as helpers when directed; assist in moving office furniture when instructed. Other duties as assigned by the Director/Assistant Director of Facilities and Grounds. REQUIRED KNOWLEDGE, SKILLS, AND ABILITIES Excellent verbal and communication skills. Excellent interpersonal and customer service skills. Excellent organizational skills and attention to detail. Excellent time management skills with a proven ability to meet deadlines. Ability to prioritize tasks. May require walking or standing for long periods. Ability to work outside for extended periods. Ability to lift and carry up to 50 lbs. Ability to operate machinery. Possess a valid driver’s license with a positive driving record. EDUCATION AND EXPERIENCE High School Diploma or Equivalent desired. Prior experience in a grounds/landscaping environment desired Apply for this Position Apply with Indeed Go back to the job list powered by"
    }
  },
